<title>USA: Skyline to buy back up to 1 million shares.</title>
<headline>Skyline to buy back up to 1 million shares.</headline>
<dateline>ELKHART, Ind. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Skyline Corp said Monday it intends to repurchase up to one million of its common shares, or about 10 percent of the total.</p>
<p>The one million shares would be in addition to about 250,000 shares which remain to be repurchased under a previous authorization to buy back 1.2 million shares.</p>
<p>Purchases will be made in the open market or in negotiated transactions. Skyline said William Blair &amp; Co will be the exclusive agent for the repurchase program.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
